# Ignore test files + the host's native libs (harper rebuilds inside docker;
# the ORT/tokenizers libs are re-fetched in CI). Without this, the host's
# glibc-2.43-built libharper_c.so would be copied into the build context
# and break the bookworm linker.
#
# Exception: the vendored harper-c Rust SOURCE (native/harper-c/) MUST be in the
# build context so the Docker `harper` stage can COPY + cargo build it. Its build
# output (target/) and any prebuilt .so/.a/.h directly under native/ stay out.
*_test.go
/bin/
/cover.out
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
native/*
!native/harper-c
native/harper-c/target
